  "missing_workload_limitation": "Because inclusion is based on jobs ending on selected days, there may be jobs active during a selected support interval whose end date is unselected and therefore absent from the dataset. This missing concurrent load is not identifiable from this dataset alone. Therefore no F2 variant may be described as actual cabinet power, complete cabinet power, or measured fleet cabinet load. The correct description is: observed reconstructed concurrent cabinet power from the public job sample.",
  "paradox_reconciliation": "Three prior observations coexist: (a) 77.9% of end_time values fall in the same UTC calendar day as date_dir; (b) many jobs have start_time on a different day from date_dir; (c) the prior audit reported 0 crossing jobs. Reconciliation: (a) and (b) are consistent \u2014 date_dir records the UTC calendar day on which a job ended; multi-hour jobs naturally start on an earlier calendar day, so start_time < date_dir is expected and not a mismatch. (c) was a post-clipping artefact: task_d_f2_reference.py clips all job intervals to support-block boundaries before building the event list. After clipping, no interval extends beyond a block boundary by construction, so a crossing check performed on clipped intervals always returns zero regardless of how many unclipped jobs actually straddle block boundaries. The pre-clipping crossing counts in this audit (total_jobs_crossing_any_start, total_jobs_crossing_any_end) are the correct figures, and they are handled correctly by the existing clip logic.",
